.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
md
- read markdown, write formatted text
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
md [ -w n ] [ file ... ]
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Md reads markdown from each file in turn (or the standard input with no
file, or where a file is -) and writes a plain-text rendering to the
standard output.  It is meant to be piped into less:
.sp
.bd
md DISKLABEL.md | less
.sp
Emphasis is overstrike: bold text is struck twice and underlined text is
struck over an underscore, so less renders it on a glass tty.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
BLOCKS
.in +5
.br
ATX and setext headings, horizontal rules, filled paragraphs, fenced code
blocks (verbatim), blockquotes, nested lists, and pipe tables with
column alignment are recognised.  Inline, **bold**, *italic* and
`code` are resolved; the backticks of a code span are dropped.  Links are
not used in the tree's documents and are not handled.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
OPTIONS
.in +5
.br
.in +10
.ti -10
-w n	Fill text to a right margin of n columns, rather than the default
72.
.in -10
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
form (1), less (1)
